SUMMARY:Guided Walking Tour of Yorkville 
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nOn **Wednesday\, July 22nd**\, **join a Gu
 ided Walking Tour of Yorkville.** Evolving from an 1800’s tollgate villa
 ge at the edge of Toronto to an upscale commercial destination\, see how t
 his iconic neighbourhood has maintained its character despite being engulf
 ed by the city. These Tours are guided by docents\, and run rain or shine.
  However\, if the forecast calls for rain\, I will make a call 3 hours pri
 or if I will show up\, as others may want to continue in the rain\, which 
 the forecast has been off a lot recently.\n\n**Prepare for the walk:**\n\n
 * Walking shoes\n* Hat\n* Sunglasses\n* Water\n\n‐‐----‐----‐‐--
 -----------‐-----------\n**COST:**\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n‐‐--
 --‐----‐‐-------------‐-----------\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes
  to confirm if you will join for food/ drinks after**\n* A reminder will b
 e sent the day before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and 
 when.\n\nRSVPs close 1 day prior and cancellations may result in a No Show
  and impact future attendance\n\n**MEETUP DETAILS:**\n**Meet at: 5:45pm at
  1 Yorkville Ave (SW corner at Yonge)**\n**Tour location: We will then joi
 n the rest of the tour group at Yorkville Library at 22 Yorkville Ave.**\n
 **Tour starts: at 6pm**\n**Tour ends:** ROM\, corner of Bloor St. and Quee
 n’s Park (100 Queen’s Park\, Toronto\n**Walk length: less than hours**
 \nAfter: Head over to a local restaurant\n\nEnjoy and please post your Com
 ments in the event after
